From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:59:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] msctf: thread manager activation flags, UI elements, single
 sinks, keystroke dispatch

ITfThreadMgrEx::ActivateEx honours TF_TMAE_NOACTIVATETIP and rejects unknown flags;
GetActiveFlags reports TF_TMF_ACTIVATED plus the flags of the first activation.
ITfUIElementMgr keeps the begun elements (ids from 1), tells the ITfUIElementSink sinks
(any of which can ask to draw the element itself) and enumerates them. ITfSourceSingle
holds one sink per client and interface (CONNECT_E_ADVISELIMIT on a second one).
ITfKeystrokeMgr TestKeyDown/TestKeyUp/KeyDown/KeyUp go to the matching preserved key
(OnPreservedKey of its owner) or else to the foreground key sink; GetPreservedKey,
Get/SetPreservedKeyDescription and SimulatePreservedKey are implemented. A preserved key
description is now null terminated.

